<title>NETHERLANDS: EU plan may feature aid for small, medium firms -official.</title>
<headline>EU plan may feature aid for small, medium firms -official.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>An European Union compromise plan on jobs growth may include a scheme to promote small and medium-sized businesses using funds from the European Investment Bank (EIB), the bank's chief spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>Spokesman Henry Marty-Gauquie told Reuters the EIB had a whole set of possible actions in mind and a special scheme for such firms was &quot;in the air&quot;.</p>
<p>He said: &quot;The bank is in a very strong  position on the capital markets and in its own financial position to give a positive response to a new definition of priorities.&quot;</p>
<p>The EIB last week reported a 1996 profit of over one billion ECU.</p>
</text>
